  "drawnOn": "A320",
  "description": "Fuselage: Fire-engine red all over, belly included. Tail: Red fin; its lower half a blue FDNY panel edged in gold (a thin red line inside the gold) along the top, a chamfered aft corner and the forward side, carrying 'FIRE DEPARTMENT' in an arc of gold capitals, 'CITY OF NEW YORK' in white and a white skyline with the twin towers along the root. The forward gold edge runs on down the aft fuselage behind the aft door, and a second gold line runs from the rudder's foot down to the tail cone; the two close in toward the belly like a badge's sides, and between them, under the skyline, the badge's white field carries FDNY's Maltese cross (blue-outlined arms, red ring). Red tail-cone tip. Engines: Red with white 'jetblue.com', polished lips. Winglets: Red wingtip fences. Titles: Large white 'jetBlue' forward; 'Blue Bravest' small below the cockpit. Artwork: FDNY panel and Maltese cross.",
