  "notes": "Drawn from left-side photos (2023-05-16, 2024-02-25); a 2021 left-side shot agrees. Redrawn 2026-11-27 from the 2014 tail close-up and the 2016 right-side photo: what wraps the aft fuselage is FDNY's Maltese cross between two thin gold lines, not a US flag; the panel is a mid blue in sunlight, lighter than navy. Small markings not drawn: an FDNY patch and a US flag by the forward door, 'Honored to support New York's Bravest' near the aft door. Re-checked 2026-11-15: 'jetBlue' placed as on the standard (measured in metres on the A321neo N2017J and checked on A320s: x 0.174-0.356 of an A320, cap 1.57 m, lowercase 0.76 of the capitals); 'jetblue.com' on the A320's nacelle x 0.43-0.79 (read off N615JB and N627JB); the name under the cockpit given its length. Re-checked 2026-11-27 (second pass): the panel is FDNY's badge, its gold edges (a red line inside them) running on down the aft fuselage and closing in toward the belly; under the skyline the badge is white, not red, round the stabilizer (both sides, 2014-2022 photos)."
}
